From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:55:42 +0000
Subject: Shorten the address bar hint to fit

The address bar hint names the search engine ("Search DuckDuckGo or
type URL"). When it is wider than the field, for example in the
toolbar of the new tab page or with a large font size, it was cut off
in the middle of a word, because an editable text field does not
ellipsize its hint.

Shorten the hint to the field width with a trailing ellipsis, and
again whenever the width changes. Screen readers still get the whole
hint.

